Package: songonsole
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Piotr Lewandowski <piotr.petexy@gmail.com>
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Depends: @SHLIB_DEPENDS@, libxkbcommon0, libegl1, ffmpeg
Recommends: xdg-desktop-portal
Suggests: libvulkan1
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Homepage: https://github.com/Petexy/songonsole
Description: a music library and player in the LineXinBar design language
 Shown as Music. Your songs, gathered from the folders you name, read for their
 tags and their artwork and laid out as a list of songs, a wall of record
 sleeves, a shelf of artists, your favourites and the queue.
 .
 Pressing a song grows its sleeve out of the row it was on into a Now Playing
 page that fills the window: the artwork as large as the screen will allow, the
 song, the artist, the album it came from, where it has got to, and what is
 coming after it. Back shrinks the page into the row it came from and the music
 keeps playing while you go on browsing.
 .
 The transport is the same row of controls on both screens, so shuffle, repeat,
 skipping, seeking and the volume are always in the same place, and the row
 along the bottom of the library is both what is playing and how to control it.
 .
 It is an ordinary Wayland application, drawn in the LineXinBar design language
 and driven from a controller, a keyboard and a pointer at once. It runs under
 GNOME or Plasma as readily as under the shell it was made for.
 .
 libxkbcommon0 and libegl1 are named here because they are opened by name at
 run time rather than linked, so nothing that reads the executable can find
 them. ffmpeg is named because ffprobe reads every file's tags and its length
 and ffmpeg lifts out its artwork — they are run as programs rather than linked,
 so nothing that reads the executable finds those either, and without them the
 library stays empty. libvulkan1 is only suggested: with a Vulkan driver present
 this draws through it, and without one it falls back to EGL.
